BUG P2: .nav-btn CSS not in shared/styles.css -- scorecard CTAs are unstyled on exam.html

Filed by: GD (nav-btn audit)
SEVERITY: P2 -- Visual regression. Scorecard CTAs '🏀 Back to Dashboard' and '🔄 Run It Back' appear as plain browser-default links.

ROOT CAUSE
.nav-btn CSS is defined ONLY in index.html inline <style> block (lines 174-184):
  .nav-btn { display: inline-block; padding: 12px 32px; font-weight: 700; border-radius: 6px; ... }
  .nav-btn.primary { background: var(--accent-red); ... }
  .nav-btn.ghost { background: transparent; ... }

exam.html loads shared/styles.css but NOT index.html's inline styles.
Result: on exam.html scorecard, all .nav-btn elements have ZERO CSS applied.

AFFECTED ELEMENTS (exam.html)
- Line 144: <a class='nav-btn ghost'> -- static 'Back to Dashboard' in exam header
- Line 1071 (JS): nav-btn primary -- '🏀 Back to Dashboard' scorecard CTA
- Lines 1076-1077 (JS): nav-btn primary + nav-btn ghost -- 'Run It Back' + '← Dashboard'

All 4 use inline style='text-decoration:none' which hides underlines but no other styling applies.

FIX: Move .nav-btn to shared/styles.css

Copy these rules from index.html lines 174-184 into shared/styles.css (after .btn-ghost section, ~line 493):

  .nav-btn {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 12px 32px;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: var(--text-base);
      border-radius: 6px;
      text-decoration: none;
      border: 2px solid transparent;
      transition: background 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
      cursor: pointer;
  }
  .nav-btn.primary {
      background: var(--accent-red);
      color: var(--text-inverse);
      border-color: var(--accent-red);
  }
  .nav-btn.primary:hover {
      background: var(--accent-red-hover);
      border-color: var(--accent-red-hover);
  }
  .nav-btn.secondary {
      background: transparent;
      color: var(--accent-navy);
      border-color: var(--accent-navy);
  }
  .nav-btn.secondary:hover {
      background: var(--accent-navy);
      color: var(--text-inverse);
  }
  .nav-btn.ghost {
      background: transparent;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      border: none;
      text-decoration: underline;
  }

After moving to shared: remove the duplicate from index.html inline styles (lines 174-184).
index.html will inherit from shared/styles.css.

VERIFY
- exam.html scorecard: 'Run It Back' button is red, 'Dashboard' link has underline/ghost style
- exam.html header: 'Back to Dashboard' renders with ghost style (no background, underlined)
- index.html: nav-btn buttons still render correctly (unchanged visual)

SCOPE: shared/styles.css (add ~8 rules) + index.html (remove inline duplicate).
